{"orgCode":"8615","name":"California Privacy Protection Agency","agencyCode":"8000","agencyName":"General Government","description":"The California Privacy Protection Agency's mission is to ensure consumers are aware of their rights, businesses are well informed of their obligations, and to vigorously enforce the law against businesses that violate consumers' privacy rights. On November 3, 2020, California voters approved Proposition 24, the California Privacy Rights Act of 2020, creating the California Privacy Protection Agency. The Agency is vested with administrative power, authority, and jurisdiction to implement and enforce the California Consumer Privacy Act of 2018, as amended, which is aimed at protecting Californians' personal information and the promotion of public awareness and understanding of the risks, rules, and rights related to the collection, use, sale, and disclosure of personal information, including the rights of minors.\n\nThe Agency also implements and enforces the Delete Act, which requires the Agency to host the state's Data Broker Registry and establish an accessible deletion mechanism through which California consumers can direct registered data brokers to delete their non-exempt personal information.\n\nThe Agency is governed by a five-member board, including the chairperson. The chairperson and one member of the board are appointed by the Governor. The Attorney General, the Senate Rules Committee, and the Speaker of the Assembly each appoint one member. These appointments must be made from among Californians with expertise in the areas of privacy, technology, and consumer rights.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":19694},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":63}},"programs":{"id":"exp/8000/8615","kind":"department","name":"California Privacy Protection Agency","code":"8615","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":19694},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":63},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":12629},"special":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":7065}},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/8615/6600","kind":"program","name":"Administration of the California Consumer Privacy Act","code":"6600","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":19694},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":12629},"special":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":7065}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":63},"description":"6600 - ADMINISTRATION OF THE CALIFORNIA CONSUMER PRIVACY ACT\n\nThe Agency implements and enforces the California Consumer Privacy Act of 2018, as amended, and has several responsibilities including: rulemaking in a highly complicated, technical, sometimes contested, and nuanced area; supporting awareness across California's diverse population of issues related to privacy and data security, including the new rights provided to them by the law; and administrative enforcement of those rights.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":19694}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/8615/6600/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":12629},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":12629}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":12629}}}},{"id":"exp/8000/8615/6600/f1030","kind":"fund","name":"Consumer Privacy Fund","code":"1030","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":1328},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":1328}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":1328}}}},{"id":"exp/8000/8615/6600/f3372","kind":"fund","name":"Data Brokers’ Registry Fund","code":"3372","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":5737},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":5737}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":5737}}}}]}],"sources":[{"label":"ebudget.ca.gov API: orgProgram/8615","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/api/budget/e/2026-27/orgProgram/8615"},{"label":"Detailed Expenditures by Program (PDF)","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/2026-27/pdf/Enacted/GovernorsBudget